Subject: JSON.stringify walks a plain object's shape instead of building its key list and looking every key up

What this does
  - in `js_json_to_str`, an ordinary (JS_CLASS_OBJECT, not exotic) object whose keys are all strings that are not array indices and none a module variable reference is walked over its shape, held with a count for the walk: each enumerable key in shape order, the value read from its slot while the object still has that shape and the property is plain data, else with JS_GetProperty; the rest (toJSON, replacer, gap, quoting) is the general loop's code

Why we need it
  JS_GetOwnPropertyNamesInternal, the key array, js_free_prop_enum and a JS_GetPropertyInternal per key were 15.5% of stringify cycles on the app-traffic benchmark. json_app stringify only: -13.3% cycles, -14.1% instructions (after 0584).

Soundness
  For such an object JS_GetOwnPropertyNames(STRING | ENUM_ONLY) is exactly the enumerable keys in shape order (integer keys, which it sorts first, and symbols are excluded by the check), and the key list is fixed when the walk starts, as the general path's array is. A value is read from its slot only when the object still has the walk's shape (no property added, deleted or reconfigured by a toJSON, replacer or getter in between) and the property is plain data, which is what JS_GetProperty returns then; otherwise JS_GetProperty is called, as the general path does. Differential, old engine vs new: 60,000 random nested values (repeated keys incl. a"b and café, deleted and non-enumerable properties) with and without indentation, and 25 cases (toJSON deleting, adding, redefining as getter or non-enumerable a later key; getters; symbols; "4294967294"/"4294967295"/"1" keys; null-prototype objects; class instances with toJSON; frozen objects; replacer arrays and functions; gaps; circular; wrappers; BigInt; inherited getters) give identical output and errors.

